##
    Insisting on an optional that turned out to be empty.

    This program compiles. 'Value()' is the way to read an optional without proving presence
    first — it insists, and throws when there is nothing there. 'HasValue()' and 'Or(...)'
    are the two ways to ask instead of insist.
##

shared model Program

    function Main()
        integer[] scores = {2, 5, 8};

        Console.WriteLine("8 is at " + Program.IndexOf(scores, 8).Value());

        # 40 is not in the set, so this one insists on nothing.
        Console.WriteLine("40 is at " + Program.IndexOf(scores, 40).Value());
    end function

    integer? function IndexOf(integer[] values, integer wanted)
        for i = 0 until values.Count()
            if values[i] == wanted
                yield i;
            end if
        end for

        integer? missing;
        yield missing;
    end function

end model
